adjudication.rationale:
In store.js.es6, the singular foreign-key hydration path still deletes the raw key only inside the `if (hydrated)` guard:
```js
} else {
  const hydrated = self._lookupSubType(...);
  if (hydrated) {
    obj[subType] = hydrated;
    delete obj[k];
  }
}
```
So the diff does not move `delete obj[k]` outside the guard for the singular case, and does not delete `category_id` when hydration returns null. (The plural `_ids` branch *does* always delete `obj[k]`, but that’s a different behavior than the finding claims.)
